  "conclusion": "The held front handle right straight leg and its sewn mouth root are the closest identified physical material to the right palm. As the palm descends, near-contact migrates down the leg to the root. The measured link7 resultant moment closely matches the lever arm to this palm contact. The fixed hand is merged into IPC link7, so the link7 wrench label does not imply the wrist shell itself is contacting cloth.",
  "root_question_positive_Y_offset": "The evidence identifies a local front right strap/root obstruction; it does not establish positive-Y offset as its sole cause. The nearest contact is+X and\u2212Y from the TCP. A negative-X path adjustment is a geometrically motivated candidate to move away from that right strap leg, but a new complete route and actual-state checks are required. Increasing descent depth along the unchanged axis continues loading this root.",
  "physical_next_step": "Keep all force, torque, soft deformation and final containment gates. A bounded lateral repositioning while the palm is still above the strap/root can be evaluated against the complete hand/strap surface and the teddy/left-arm route. Do not assume a final-pose offset or a faster/slower downward push resolves the caught strap. Alternatively redesign the approach/held-handle pose so the palm can descend without feeding the held strap underneath it.",
  "limitations": [
    "Native link7 IPC matrices are not saved. Same-time complete frames contain only translation/rotation/affine deviation magnitudes, so mesh distances use FK and report a pose-error bound. At true failed soft frame even this same-time deviation is unavailable; previous frame is15ms earlier.",
    "The frozen original collision mesh surface is used. Native imported rigid collision processing may convexify or decimate meshes; this report does not claim exact native IPC surface reconstruction.",
    "Distances query cloth triangle vertices, all edge midpoints and centroids and all bear vertices. Positive samples do not prove whole-surface separation, continuous clearance, or absence of narrow contact.",
    "Robot-link aggregate native wrench does not identify the colliding material pair. Geometric coincidence with a torque trend is evidence, not pairwise force attribution.",
    "No alternate trajectory, offset, release action, material, or protection threshold is changed or certified.",
    "Convexification correspondence removes the main original-surface ambiguity for this hand mesh; same-time native affine matrices remain unavailable.",
    "No new offset, timing, orientation or control policy has been planned or tested here.",
    "The scene-local aggregate wrench cannot distinguish held front strip from simultaneously approaching front panel at a few millimetres; near-contact at the stitched root may involve both."
  ]
